IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-offence`
IMPORT `ccc7-s184-applications`

-- ccc7-s186-authorizations.l4 -- sections 186 (when the judge may give an authorization), 186.1 (longer periods for criminal organization and terrorism offences), 188 (urgent applications to specially appointed judges),
-- 188.1 (execution anywhere in Canada) and 188.2 (no civil or criminal liability) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI. (Section 187 is in ccc7-s187-packet.l4.)
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- What these sections mean to the person in the seat: what a judge had to be satisfied of before an authorization could be given about them (and when the "other methods have failed" condition is waived), what the authorization had to say,
-- how long it could last, what is barred at a lawyer's office, and who is shielded from liability for acting on it.
-- Grants named "may" with an "if" gate answer NOTHING when the gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12); "may ... where" grants answer JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) and are listed for a lawyer (fork register F11); a bar or a requirement not met is JUST FALSE.

§ `Section 186 -- Judge to be satisfied`

-- 186(1.1): "Notwithstanding paragraph (1)(b), that paragraph does not apply where the judge is satisfied that the application for an authorization is in relation to (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13;
-- (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization; (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or (c) a terrorism offence."
-- src:3868 | Exception for criminal organizations and terrorism offences
-- src:3869 | (1.1) Notwithstanding paragraph (1)(b), that paragraph does not apply where the judge is satisfied that the application for an authorization is in relation to
-- src:3870 | (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13;
-- src:3871 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- src:3872 | (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or
-- src:3873 | (c) a terrorism offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(1.1) (src:3868-3873)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the application is in relation to the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence the application is in relation to` IS A `s 183 provision of an Act`
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied that the application is in relation to the offence in question`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that paragraph does not apply where the judge is satisfied that the application for an authorization is in relation to"
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that paragraph does not apply where the judge is satisfied that the application for an authorization is in relation to"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a criminal organization, or the offence a terrorism offence, is for another section and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the offence the application is in relation to`'s `section`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (`the offence the application is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Criminal Code`)
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 52 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.111 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.13)
        `limb (b.1)` MEANS
            (`the offence the application is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`)
            AND (`the offence the application is in relation to`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 20 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.3 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.4)
        `the limbs` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (a)`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group`, `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (b.1)`
                    , `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`)

-- 186(1): "An authorization under this section may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied (a) that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to do so; and (b) that other investigative procedures
-- have been tried and have failed, other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed or the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation of the offence using only other investigative procedures."
-- A grant ("may be given") with an "if" gate: a failed gate is NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12). Paragraph (b) is waived where subsection (1.1) says it does not apply.
-- src:3864 | Judge to be satisfied
-- src:3865 | 186 (1) An authorization under this section may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied
-- src:3866 | (a) that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to do so; and
-- src:3867 | (b) that other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed, other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed or the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation of the offence using only other investigative procedures.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(1) (src:3864-3867)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to give the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation of the offence using only other investigative procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to give the authorization`
       AND (   `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed`
            OR `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed`
            OR `the judge is satisfied that the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation of the offence using only other investigative procedures`
            OR (`s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied"

-- 186(2): "No authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at the office or residence of a solicitor, or at any other place ordinarily used by a solicitor and by other solicitors for the purpose of consultation with clients,
-- unless the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor, any other solicitor practising with him, any person employed by him or any other such solicitor or a member of the
-- solicitor’s household has been or is about to become a party to an offence." The function is named for the bar: JUST TRUE = the bar applies (no authorization may be given); JUST FALSE = the "unless" is met; NOTHING = not a place the bar speaks to
-- (a scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)). "Solicitor" is the section 183 term (by province): a MAYBE BOOLEAN input.
-- src:3874 | Where authorization not to be given
-- src:3875 | (2) No authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at the office or residence of a solicitor, or at any other place ordinarily used by a solicitor and by other solicitors for the purpose of consultation with clients, unless the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor, any other solicitor practising with him, any person employed by him or any other such solicitor or a member of the solicitor’s household has been or is about to become a party to an offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(2) (src:3874-3875)
GIVEN `the person whose office or residence it is, or who ordinarily uses the place, is a solicitor, by s 183 solicitor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the place is the office or residence of a solicitor, or any other place ordinarily used by a solicitor and by other solicitors for the purpose of consultation with clients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor, a solicitor practising with him, a person employed by him or a member of the solicitor’s household has been or is about to become a party to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the place is the office or residence of a solicitor, or any other place ordinarily used by a solicitor and by other solicitors for the purpose of consultation with clients`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the office or residence of a solicitor, or at any other place ordinarily used by a solicitor and by other solicitors for the purpose of consultation with clients"
        IF `the person whose office or residence it is, or who ordinarily uses the place, is a solicitor, by s 183 solicitor` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the office or residence of a solicitor"
        IF `the person whose office or residence it is, or who ordinarily uses the place, is a solicitor, by s 183 solicitor` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a "solicitor" is for section 183 and is not covered
        IF `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor, a solicitor practising with him, a person employed by him or a member of the solicitor’s household has been or is about to become a party to an offence`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 186(3): "Where an authorization is given in relation to the interception of private communications at a place described in subsection (2), the judge by whom the authorization is given shall include therein such terms and conditions as he considers
-- advisable to protect privileged communications between solicitors and clients." The duty, as two functions: whether the judge is bound (JUST FALSE where the "Where" fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)), and whether it has been kept.
-- src:3876 | Terms and conditions
-- src:3877 | (3) Where an authorization is given in relation to the interception of private communications at a place described in subsection (2), the judge by whom the authorization is given shall include therein such terms and conditions as he considers advisable to protect privileged communications between solicitors and clients.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(3) (src:3876-3877)
GIVEN `an authorization is given in relation to the interception of private communications at a place described in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(3) the judge is bound to include terms and conditions to protect privileged communications` MEANS
    IF `an authorization is given in relation to the interception of private communications at a place described in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an authorization is given in relation to the interception of private communications at a place described in subsection (2)"

-- src:3876 | Terms and conditions
-- src:3877 | (3) Where an authorization is given in relation to the interception of private communications at a place described in subsection (2), the judge by whom the authorization is given shall include therein such terms and conditions as he considers advisable to protect privileged communications between solicitors and clients.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(3) (src:3876-3877)
GIVEN `s 186(3) bound` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge included such terms and conditions as he considers advisable to protect privileged communications between solicitors and clients` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(3) the judge has included the terms and conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 186(3) bound` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN IF `the judge included such terms and conditions as he considers advisable to protect privileged communications between solicitors and clients`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall include therein such terms and conditions as he considers advisable to protect privileged communications between solicitors and clients"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty binds only where the authorization concerns a place described in subsection (2)

-- 186(4)(e): "be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein", subject to section 186.1 ("Notwithstanding paragraphs 184.2(4)(e) and 186(4)(e) and subsection 186(7)").
-- src:3878 | Content and limitation of authorization
-- src:3879 | (4) An authorization shall
-- src:3880 | (a) state the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted;
-- src:3881 | (b) state the type of private communication that may be intercepted;
-- src:3882 | (c) state the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describe the place at which private communications may be intercepted, if a general description of that place can be given, and generally describe the manner of interception that may be used;
-- src:3883 | (d) contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and
-- src:3884 | (e) be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(4) (src:3878-3884)
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the period ends` IS A DATE
      `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the day the period ends` MINUS Day `the day the period begins`) PLUS 1 AT MOST 60
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 186.1 lets the period exceed sixty days is for that section and is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein"

-- 186(4): "An authorization shall (a) state the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted; (b) state the type of private communication that may be intercepted; (c) state the identity of the persons, if known, ...,
-- generally describe the place ... and generally describe the manner of interception that may be used; (d) contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and (e) be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein."
-- src:3878 | Content and limitation of authorization
-- src:3879 | (4) An authorization shall
-- src:3880 | (a) state the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted;
-- src:3881 | (b) state the type of private communication that may be intercepted;
-- src:3882 | (c) state the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describe the place at which private communications may be intercepted, if a general description of that place can be given, and generally describe the manner of interception that may be used;
-- src:3883 | (d) contain such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and
-- src:3884 | (e) be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(4) (src:3878-3884)
GIVEN `the authorization states the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization states the type of private communication that may be intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization states the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describes the place and generally describes the manner of interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization contains such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 186(4)(e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(4) the authorization has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the authorization states the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted` AND `the authorization states the type of private communication that may be intercepted` AND `the authorization states the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describes the place and generally describes the manner of interception` AND `the authorization contains such terms and conditions as the judge considers advisable in the public interest`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorization shall"
        OTHERWISE `s 186(4)(e)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("not exceeding sixty days"); NOTHING when section 186.1 is not covered

-- 186(5): "The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or the Attorney General, as the case may be, may designate a person or persons who may intercept private communications under authorizations."
-- src:3885 | Persons designated
-- src:3886 | (5) The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or the Attorney General, as the case may be, may designate a person or persons who may intercept private communications under authorizations.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(5) (src:3885-3886)
GIVEN `the person has been designated by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or the Attorney General, as the case may be, to intercept private communications under authorizations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(5) the person may intercept private communications under authorizations` MEANS
    IF `the person has been designated by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or the Attorney General, as the case may be, to intercept private communications under authorizations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may designate a person or persons who may intercept private communications under authorizations"

-- 186(5.1): "For greater certainty, an authorization that permits interception by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device includes the authority to install, maintain or remove the device covertly." An "includes" provision.
DECLARE `s 186(5.1) act on the device` IS ONE OF
    `s 186(5.1) installing the device covertly`
    `s 186(5.1) maintaining the device covertly`
    `s 186(5.1) removing the device covertly`
    `s 186(5.1) an act on the device that is none of those`

-- src:3887 | Installation and removal of device
-- src:3888 | (5.1) For greater certainty, an authorization that permits interception by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device includes the authority to install, maintain or remove the device covertly.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(5.1) (src:3887-3888)
GIVEN `the authorization permits interception by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 186(5.1) act on the device`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(5.1) the authorization includes the authority to do the act on the device` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the authorization permits interception by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an authorization that permits interception by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device"
        IF act EQUALS `s 186(5.1) an act on the device that is none of those`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the authority to install, maintain or remove the device covertly"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 186(5.2): "On an ex parte application, in writing, supported by affidavit, the judge who gave an authorization referred to in subsection (5.1) or any other judge having jurisdiction to give such an authorization may give a further authorization for the
-- covert removal of the electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device after the expiry of the original authorization (a) under any terms or conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and (b) during any specified period
-- of not more than sixty days." A grant: outside its own limits it is NOT COVERED.
-- src:3889 | Removal after expiry of authorization
-- src:3890 | (5.2) On an ex parte application, in writing, supported by affidavit, the judge who gave an authorization referred to in subsection (5.1) or any other judge having jurisdiction to give such an authorization may give a further authorization for the covert removal of the electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device after the expiry of the original authorization
-- src:3891 | (a) under any terms or conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and
-- src:3892 | (b) during any specified period of not more than sixty days.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(5.2) (src:3889-3892)
GIVEN `the application is ex parte, in writing, and supported by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is the judge who gave the authorization or any other judge having jurisdiction to give such an authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further authorization is for the covert removal of the device after the expiry of the original authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the specified period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the specified period ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(5.2) a further authorization for the covert removal of the device may be given` MEANS
    IF `the application is ex parte, in writing, and supported by affidavit`
       AND `the judge is the judge who gave the authorization or any other judge having jurisdiction to give such an authorization`
       AND `the further authorization is for the covert removal of the device after the expiry of the original authorization`
       AND ((Day `the day the specified period ends` MINUS Day `the day the specified period begins`) PLUS 1 AT MOST 60)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during any specified period of not more than sixty days"

-- 186(6): "Renewals of an authorization may be given by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 on receipt by him or her of an ex parte application in writing signed by the Attorney General of the province
-- in which the application is made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness — or an agent specially designated in writing for the purposes of section 185 by the Minister or the Attorney General, as the case may be — accompanied by an
-- affidavit of a peace officer or public officer deposing to the following matters: (a) the reason and period for which the renewal is required, (b) full particulars ... of interceptions, and (c) the number of instances ..., and supported by such other
-- information as the judge may require."
-- src:3893 | Renewal of authorization
-- src:3894 | (6) Renewals of an authorization may be given by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 on receipt by him or her of an ex parte application in writing signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application is made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness — or an agent specially designated in writing for the purposes of section 185 by the Minister or the Attorney General, as the case may be — accompanied by an affidavit of a peace officer or public officer deposing to the following matters:
-- src:3895 | (a) the reason and period for which the renewal is required,
-- src:3896 | (b) full particulars, together with times and dates, when interceptions, if any, were made or attempted under the authorization, and any information that has been obtained by any interception, and
-- src:3897 | (c) the number of instances, if any, on which, to the knowledge and belief of the deponent, an application has been made under this subsection in relation to the same authorization and on which the application was withdrawn or no renewal was given, the date on which each application was made and the name of the judge to whom each application was made,
-- src:3898 | and supported by such other information as the judge may require.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(6) (src:3893-3898)
GIVEN `the renewal is given by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is ex parte and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application is made, the Minister, or an agent specially designated in writing for the purposes of section 185` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accompanied by an affidavit of a peace officer or public officer deposing to the reason and period, the particulars of the interceptions and the number of earlier applications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is supported by such other information as the judge may require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(6) a renewal of an authorization may be given on the application` MEANS
    IF `the renewal is given by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552`
       AND `the application is ex parte and in writing`
       AND `it is signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application is made, the Minister, or an agent specially designated in writing for the purposes of section 185`
       AND `it is accompanied by an affidavit of a peace officer or public officer deposing to the reason and period, the particulars of the interceptions and the number of earlier applications`
       AND `it is supported by such other information as the judge may require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on receipt by him or her of an ex parte application in writing signed by"

-- 186(7): "A renewal of an authorization may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that any of the circumstances described in subsection (1) still obtain, but no renewal shall be for a period exceeding sixty days."
-- src:3899 | Renewal
-- src:3900 | (7) A renewal of an authorization may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that any of the circumstances described in subsection (1) still obtain, but no renewal shall be for a period exceeding sixty days.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(7) (src:3899-3900)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that any of the circumstances described in subsection (1) still obtain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(7) a renewal of an authorization may be given` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that any of the circumstances described in subsection (1) still obtain`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that any of the circumstances described in subsection (1) still obtain"

-- src:3899 | Renewal
-- src:3900 | (7) A renewal of an authorization may be given if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that any of the circumstances described in subsection (1) still obtain, but no renewal shall be for a period exceeding sixty days.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(7) (src:3899-3900)
GIVEN `the day the renewal begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the renewal ends` IS A DATE
      `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(7) the renewal is for a period within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the day the renewal ends` MINUS Day `the day the renewal begins`) PLUS 1 AT MOST 60
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 186.1 lets the renewal exceed sixty days is for that section and is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no renewal shall be for a period exceeding sixty days"

-- 186(8): the same related warrant or order as 184.2(5) (the list of sections is identical: 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2), for an authorization given under this section.
-- src:3901 | Related warrant or order
-- src:3902 | (8) A judge who gives an authorization under this section may, at the same time, issue a warrant or make an order under any of sections 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2 if the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization.
@ref Criminal Code s 186(8) (src:3901-3902)
GIVEN `the warrant or order requested` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the judge gives the authorization under section 186 and acts at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(8) the judge may at the same time issue the related warrant or make the related order` MEANS
    IF `s 184.2(5) the section is one of those the subsection lists` `the warrant or order requested`
       AND `the judge gives the authorization under section 186 and acts at the same time`
       AND `the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sections the subsection lists are not said to be the only ones, and a failed "if" gate on a grant is not a "may not"

§ `Section 186.1 -- Time limitation in relation to criminal organizations and terrorism offences`

-- 186.1: "Notwithstanding paragraphs 184.2(4)(e) and 186(4)(e) and subsection 186(7), an authorization or any renewal of an authorization may be valid for one or more periods specified in the authorization exceeding sixty days, each not exceeding
-- one year, where the authorization is in relation to (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13; (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or (c) a terrorism offence."
-- A "may ... where" grant: a failed "where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) (listed for a lawyer, F11). This function answers whether the offence is one the section lists; it is the input `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` of 184.2(4)(e), 186(4)(e) and 186(7).
-- src:3903 | Time limitation in relation to criminal organizations and terrorism offences
-- src:3904 | 186.1 Notwithstanding paragraphs 184.2(4)(e) and 186(4)(e) and subsection 186(7), an authorization or any renewal of an authorization may be valid for one or more periods specified in the authorization exceeding sixty days, each not exceeding one year, where the authorization is in relation to
-- src:3905 | (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13;
-- src:3906 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- src:3907 | (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or
-- src:3908 | (c) a terrorism offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 186.1 (src:3903-3908)
GIVEN `the offence the authorization is in relation to` IS A `s 183 provision of an Act`
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the authorization is in relation to"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a criminal organization, or the offence a terrorism offence, is for another section and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the offence the authorization is in relation to`'s `section`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (`the offence the authorization is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Criminal Code`)
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 52 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.111 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.13)
        `limb (b.1)` MEANS
            (`the offence the authorization is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`)
            AND (`the offence the authorization is in relation to`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 20 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.3 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.4)
        `the limbs` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (a)`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group`, `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (b.1)`
                    , `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`)

-- 186.1: "each not exceeding one year". A period of one year beginning on a day ends the day before its anniversary, both ends counted (1 March 2025 to 28 February 2026). A period longer than one year is outside the grant: NOT COVERED.
-- src:3903 | Time limitation in relation to criminal organizations and terrorism offences
-- src:3904 | 186.1 Notwithstanding paragraphs 184.2(4)(e) and 186(4)(e) and subsection 186(7), an authorization or any renewal of an authorization may be valid for one or more periods specified in the authorization exceeding sixty days, each not exceeding one year, where the authorization is in relation to
@ref Criminal Code s 186.1 (src:3903-3904)
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the period ends` IS A DATE
      `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186.1 the authorization or renewal may be valid for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the authorization is in relation to"
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is one the section lists is not covered
        IF (Day `the day the period ends`) AT MOST ((Day (`add years` `the day the period begins` 1)) MINUS 1)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each not exceeding one year"

§ `Section 188 -- Applications to specially appointed judges`

DECLARE `s 188(1) who designated the peace officer` IS ONE OF
    `s 188(1) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    `s 188(1) the Attorney General of a province`
    `s 188(1) someone else`

-- 188(1): "Notwithstanding section 185, an application made under that section for an authorization may be made ex parte to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, or a judge as defined in section 552, designated from time to time by the
-- Chief Justice, by a peace officer specially designated in writing, by name or otherwise, for the purposes of this section by (a) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, if the offence is one in respect of which proceedings, if any,
-- may be instituted by the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada, or (b) the Attorney General of a province, in respect of any other offence in the province, if the urgency of the situation requires
-- interception of private communications to commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186." A grant with an "if" gate: NOTHING when it fails.
-- src:3941 | Applications to specially appointed judges
-- src:3942 | 188 (1) Notwithstanding section 185, an application made under that section for an authorization may be made ex parte to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, or a judge as defined in section 552, designated from time to time by the Chief Justice, by a peace officer specially designated in writing, by name or otherwise, for the purposes of this section by
-- src:3943 | (a) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, if the offence is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted by the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada, or
-- src:3944 | (b) the Attorney General of a province, in respect of any other offence in the province,
-- src:3945 | if the urgency of the situation requires interception of private communications to commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186.
@ref Criminal Code s 188(1) (src:3941-3945)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte to a judge designated from time to time by the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      designator IS A `s 188(1) who designated the peace officer`
      `the offence is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted by the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is specially designated in writing, by name or otherwise, for the purposes of section 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the urgency of the situation requires interception of private communications to commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(1) an application for an authorization may be made to a specially appointed judge` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte to a judge designated from time to time by the Chief Justice`
       AND `the peace officer is specially designated in writing, by name or otherwise, for the purposes of section 188`
       AND `the urgency of the situation requires interception of private communications to commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186`
       AND (CONSIDER designator
            WHEN `s 188(1) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` THEN `the offence is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted by the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
            WHEN `s 188(1) the Attorney General of a province` THEN NOT `the offence is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted by the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
            WHEN `s 188(1) someone else` THEN FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the urgency of the situation requires interception of private communications to commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186"

-- 188(2): "Where the judge to whom an application is made pursuant to subsection (1) is satisfied that the urgency of the situation requires that interception of private communications commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence,
-- be obtained under section 186, he may, on such terms and conditions, if any, as he considers advisable, give an authorization in writing for a period of up to thirty-six hours." A "may ... where" grant: a failed "where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's
-- ruling (b) (F11); a period over thirty-six hours is outside "up to thirty-six hours" (NOTHING). The core's Length of time has no hours: the period is a number of hours.
-- src:3946 | Authorizations in emergency
-- src:3947 | (2) Where the judge to whom an application is made pursuant to subsection (1) is satisfied that the urgency of the situation requires that interception of private communications commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186, he may, on such terms and conditions, if any, as he considers advisable, give an authorization in writing for a period of up to thirty-six hours.
@ref Criminal Code s 188(2) (src:3946-3947)
GIVEN `the judge to whom an application is made pursuant to subsection (1) is satisfied that the urgency of the situation requires that interception commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the authorization, in hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(2) the judge may give an authorization for a period of up to thirty-six hours` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge to whom an application is made pursuant to subsection (1) is satisfied that the urgency of the situation requires that interception commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the judge to whom an application is made pursuant to subsection (1) is satisfied that the urgency of the situation requires that interception of private communications commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186"
        IF `the authorization is given in writing` AND (`the period of the authorization, in hours` AT MOST 36)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "give an authorization in writing for a period of up to thirty-six hours"

-- 188(4): "In this section, Chief Justice means (a) in the Province of Ontario, the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court; (b) in the Province of Quebec, the Chief Justice of the Superior Court; (c) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia,
-- Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, in Yukon and in the Northwest Territories, the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court; (d) in the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench;
-- (e) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 6]; (f) in Nunavut, the Chief Justice of the Nunavut Court of Justice." All thirteen provinces and territories are named, so the function answers a value.
DECLARE `s 188(4) Chief Justice` IS ONE OF
    `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court`
    `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Superior Court`
    `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- src:3949 | Definition of Chief Justice
-- src:3950 | (4) In this section, Chief Justice means
-- src:3951 | (a) in the Province of Ontario, the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court;
-- src:3952 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, the Chief Justice of the Superior Court;
-- src:3953 | (c) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, in Yukon and in the Northwest Territories, the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court;
-- src:3954 | (d) in the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench;
-- src:3955 | (e) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 6]
-- src:3956 | (f) in Nunavut, the Chief Justice of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 188(4) (src:3949-3956)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A `s 188(4) Chief Justice`
`s 188(4) Chief Justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER province
    WHEN Ontario THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court`
    WHEN Quebec THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Superior Court`
    WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `British Columbia` THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN Yukon THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Manitoba THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Saskatchewan THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Alberta THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Nunavut THEN `s 188(4) the Chief Justice of the Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- 188(5): "The trial judge may deem inadmissible the evidence obtained by means of an interception of a private communication pursuant to a subsequent authorization given under this section, where he finds that the application for the subsequent
-- authorization was based on the same facts, and involved the interception of the private communications of the same person or persons, or related to the same offence, on which the application for the original authorization was based."
-- A "may ... where" grant: a failed "where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) (F11). FORK (F12): "based on the same facts, and involved ... the same person or persons, or related to the same offence" is read as the same facts AND
-- (the same persons OR the same offence); the other reading is (the same facts AND the same persons) OR the same offence.
-- src:3957 | Inadmissibility of evidence
-- src:3958 | (5) The trial judge may deem inadmissible the evidence obtained by means of an interception of a private communication pursuant to a subsequent authorization given under this section, where he finds that the application for the subsequent authorization was based on the same facts, and involved the interception of the private communications of the same person or persons, or related to the same offence, on which the application for the original authorization was based.
@ref Criminal Code s 188(5) (src:3957-3958)
GIVEN `the evidence was obtained by means of an interception pursuant to a subsequent authorization given under section 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial judge finds that the application for the subsequent authorization was based on the same facts as the application for the original authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial judge finds that it involved the interception of the private communications of the same person or persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial judge finds that it related to the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(5) the trial judge may deem the evidence inadmissible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence was obtained by means of an interception pursuant to a subsequent authorization given under section 188`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the evidence obtained by means of an interception of a private communication pursuant to a subsequent authorization given under this section"
        IF `the trial judge finds that the application for the subsequent authorization was based on the same facts as the application for the original authorization`
           AND (`the trial judge finds that it involved the interception of the private communications of the same person or persons` OR `the trial judge finds that it related to the same offence`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where he finds that the application for the subsequent authorization was based on the same facts"

-- 188(6): "A judge who gives an authorization under this section may, at the same time, issue a warrant or make an order under any of sections 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2 if the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant
-- or order is related to the execution of the authorization, that the urgency of the situation requires the warrant or the order and that it can be reasonably executed or complied with within 36 hours."
-- src:3959 | Related warrant or order
-- src:3960 | (6) A judge who gives an authorization under this section may, at the same time, issue a warrant or make an order under any of sections 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2 if the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization, that the urgency of the situation requires the warrant or the order and that it can be reasonably executed or complied with within 36 hours.
@ref Criminal Code s 188(6) (src:3959-3960)
GIVEN `the warrant or order requested` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the judge gives the authorization under section 188 and acts at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the urgency of the situation requires the warrant or the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that it can be reasonably executed or complied with within 36 hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(6) the judge may at the same time issue the related warrant or make the related order` MEANS
    IF `s 184.2(5) the section is one of those the subsection lists` `the warrant or order requested`
       AND `the judge gives the authorization under section 188 and acts at the same time`
       AND `the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization`
       AND `the judge is of the opinion that the urgency of the situation requires the warrant or the order`
       AND `the judge is of the opinion that it can be reasonably executed or complied with within 36 hours`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sections the subsection lists are not said to be the only ones, and a failed "if" gate on a grant is not a "may not"

§ `Section 188.1 -- Execution in Canada`

-- 188.1: "An authorization given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the authorization must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed."
-- src:3961 | Execution in Canada
-- src:3962 | 188.1 An authorization given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the authorization must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 188.1 (src:3961-3962)
GIVEN `the authorization was given under section 184.2, 186 or 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188.1 the authorization may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the authorization was given under section 184.2, 186 or 188` AND `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An authorization given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 may be executed at any place in Canada"

-- src:3961 | Execution in Canada
-- src:3962 | 188.1 An authorization given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the authorization must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 188.1 (src:3961-3962)
GIVEN `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the authorization is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188.1 the peace officer who executes the authorization has the authority the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the authorization is executed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any peace officer who executes the authorization must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed"

§ `Section 188.2 -- No civil or criminal liability`

-- 188.2: "No person who acts in accordance with an authorization or under section 184.1 or 184.4 or who aids, in good faith, a person who he or she believes on reasonable grounds is acting in accordance with an authorization or under one of those sections
-- incurs any criminal or civil liability for anything reasonably done further to the authorization or to that section." The function is named for the immunity: JUST TRUE = the person incurs no criminal or civil liability; a person outside the
-- section's words is NOT COVERED (the section does not say they incur liability).
-- src:3963 | No civil or criminal liability
-- src:3964 | 188.2 No person who acts in accordance with an authorization or under section 184.1 or 184.4 or who aids, in good faith, a person who he or she believes on reasonable grounds is acting in accordance with an authorization or under one of those sections incurs any criminal or civil liability for anything reasonably done further to the authorization or to that section.
@ref Criminal Code s 188.2 (src:3963-3964)
GIVEN `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts under section 184.1 or 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person aids, in good faith, a person whom he or she believes on reasonable grounds is acting in accordance with an authorization or under section 184.1 or 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was reasonably done further to the authorization or to that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188.2 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the route` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it was reasonably done further to the authorization or to that section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "incurs any criminal or civil liability for anything reasonably done further to the authorization or to that section"
    WHERE
        `the route` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization`, `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person acts in accordance with that instrument`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person acts under section 184.1 or 184.4`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person aids, in good faith, a person whom he or she believes on reasonable grounds is acting in accordance with an authorization or under section 184.1 or 184.4`)
